 "note": "Hand data for tools/painted_rooms.py. Room-local pixels (each room is its picture size, 512x512 since M4b). exits (M4d): the sides where the picture's path reaches the middle of the edge; the tool writes an exit point (warp spot) on the open ground nearest that edge's middle, or nearest hints[side]. Which exits are joined is decided every game session by RoomLayout (scripts/rules/room_layout.gd; its FALLBACK_LINKS are the fixed M4b links, used only when no random layout passes its checks); an exit left unjoined is a dead end with no warp. edits: walk/block pixel rects. monsters: kind/level/count (M3g); in play a forest room's groups use the level of its distance from c1r1 in the session layout (scripts/rules/room_levels.gd, M4d addendum), a group 1 level above the room's first group keeps +1, so 'level' here only marks that +1 (x1..x3 use 5 as a placeholder base); groups of <=6 are placed by the tool unless 'at' is given. name: the room's Thai name (exit labels, M4c); arena: true for a boss arena (red exit label). monster_sets (e0): the arena sets in level order (w1, e0, e2, w3 of M3f); 'monsters' is the default set. grid: the room's place on the debug sheet (c?r? rooms use their id). near_arrival_ok (M4d addendum 2; x1, x2): the room's groups are placed by hand ('at') closer to the warp arrivals than their aggro range (monsters are calm 1 s on arrival), but never nearer than 48 px; the tool moves an 'at' home to the nearest cell whose whole spawn ring (radius wolf.pack_ring) is on open ground.",
